I think this is the same as #15715
This could be fixed by changing how the filter in here works:

https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/5ec5d1daceaab23c8ffa9ae32b40f53120f4609e/packages/opencode/src/provider/transform.ts#L54

instead of anthropic provider, maybe we could use something that checks the model name too. e.g.

```
function claude(model: Provider.Model) {
    if (model.providerID === "anthropic") return true
    return [model.id, model.api.id].some((item) => {
      const id = item.toLowerCase()
      return id.includes("claude") || id.includes("anthropic")
    })
  }

```
then
`if(claude(model)) ...`

although you probably have a Claude detection logic for prompt selection already.

This affects another provider I'm using (databricks api endpoint of claude)

Solution:

Configure the DeepSeek model with:

```json
{
  "provider": {
    "deepseek": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "DeepSeek",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1",
        "apiKey": "{env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}"
      },
      "models": {
        "deepseek-reasoner": {
          "name": "DeepSeek Reasoner",
          "interleaved": {
            "field": "reasoning_content"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The key part is:

```json
"interleaved": {
  "field": "reasoning_content"
}
```

After adding this and restarting OpenCode, the issue was resolved.

